<title>THAILAND: Thailand Jan-May oil demand rises 8.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Thailand Jan-May oil demand rises 8.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's petroleum demand in the first five months of 1997 grew 8.5 percent year-on-year to 956,120 barrels per day (bPd), state-run Petroleum Authority of Thailand said on Monday.</p>
<p>The demand for indigenous natural gas rose 33.8 percent to reach 198,950 bpd, while consumption of refined products averaged 757,180 bpd, an increase of 3.4 percent over the previous year, PTT said.</p>
<p>PTT detailed petroleum use and procurement in the first five months as follows (bpd):</p>
<p>Total consumption	  Jan-March 1997	 Change from 1996</p>
<p>Gas oil (diesel)		   328,840	     up   7.7 pct</p>
<p>Fuel oil			     160,360	     dn  10.7 pct</p>
<p>Gasoline			     128,770	     up   8.3 pct</p>
<p>Aviation				62,970	     up   5.2 pct</p>
<p>Liquefied petroleum gas	   55,730	     up   7.5 pct</p>
<p>Kerosene				 1,620	     dn   9.5 pct</p>
<p>Natural gas			  198,950	     up  33.8 pct</p>
<p>Bitumen				 12,770	     up  33.4 pct</p>
<p>Lubricants			     6,120	     up  10.1 pct</p>
<p>TOTAL				  956,120	     up   8.5 pct</p>
<p>Total procurement</p>
<p>Imported crude oil		 744,320	     up  32.3 pct</p>
<p>Refined product		     71,070	     dn  64.4 pct</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
